# TextFSM template for `show interfaces` on Cisco Catalyst 2950 EI.
# Single source for get_interfaces, get_interfaces_ip and
# get_interfaces_counters (ADDR/MASKLEN are empty for interfaces without an IP).
# Verified: IOS 12.1(22)EA9, WS-C2950G-48-EI.
Value Required INTERFACE (\S+)
Value LINK_STATUS (.+?)
Value PROTOCOL_STATUS (\S+)
Value MAC ([0-9a-fA-F]{4}\.[0-9a-fA-F]{4}\.[0-9a-fA-F]{4})
Value DESCRIPTION (.+?)
Value ADDR (\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+)
Value MASKLEN (\d+)
Value MTU (\d+)
Value BW (\d+)
Value RX_DISCARDS (\d+)
Value TX_DISCARDS (\d+)
Value RX_OCTETS (\d+)
Value RX_BROADCAST (\d+)
Value RX_MULTICAST (\d+)
Value RX_ERRORS (\d+)
Value TX_OCTETS (\d+)
Value TX_ERRORS (\d+)

Start
  ^\S+ is .+, line protocol is .+ -> Continue.Record
  ^${INTERFACE} is ${LINK_STATUS}, line protocol is ${PROTOCOL_STATUS}
  ^\s+Hardware is .+, address is ${MAC}
  ^\s+Description:\s+${DESCRIPTION}\s*$$
  ^\s+Internet address is ${ADDR}/${MASKLEN}
  ^\s+MTU ${MTU} bytes, BW ${BW} Kbit
  ^\s+Input queue:\s+\d+/\d+/${RX_DISCARDS}/\d+ .*Total output drops:\s+${TX_DISCARDS}
  ^\s+\d+ packets input, ${RX_OCTETS} bytes
  ^\s+Received ${RX_BROADCAST} broadcasts \(${RX_MULTICAST} .*
  ^\s+${RX_ERRORS} input errors,
  ^\s+\d+ packets output, ${TX_OCTETS} bytes
  ^\s+${TX_ERRORS} output errors,
